WEBVTT

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.870
"Eternal Midnight"

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.290
On mornings that I can't see you

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.380
Spicy mint tea

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.050
For brunch, a marmalade muffin

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.260
For its bitterness
matches my mood

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.930
My sighs are stardust

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.220
Just like our own Milky Way

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.890
I can never catch up to your back

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.150
Look, the twilight is
sneaking up on us

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.440
The distance to get to you

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.780
Is like an eternal midnight blue...

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.990
Wh-Wh-Why is it
on the floor again?

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.370
Anyway, don't read it!

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.950
Don't sneak up on me, Twilight!

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.830
I hate you... dummy...
sigh... stardust!

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.540
Don't read things
without permission!

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.350
Hey, guys!

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:36.560
Let's go to the beach!

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.810
Where'd that come from?

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.610
Well, you know, summer
vacation's almost here, right?

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:45.320
Sure, there are
incidents and all,

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.570
but you gotta have fun in
the summer, or it'll go to waste!

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.910
Well, good point. And we did
just get our licenses, right?

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.910
Yes. I'd like to take a long trip!

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:54.830
Right?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.500
We can ask Risette, too,
when she's all better.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.620
Good idea.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.170
You should come
with us, too, Marie-chan!

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.670
Well, why not?

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.300
I've never been to the beach.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.050
Hey, dude, seriously?

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.430
Shut up, old guy.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.180
O-O-Old guy?

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.510
Then you've got to go, okay?

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:16.770
But do you mind that place
being your first-ever beach?

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:17.930
It should be fine.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:22.190
The important thing is not where
you go, but who you go with, right?

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.770
Who are you, Mr. Cool?

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.440
Hey, Marie-chan!

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.320
If you've never been to the beach,
does that mean you don't have a swimsuit?

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.530
Swimsuit?

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:32.870
Don't have one.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:34.450
Yes!

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:36.200
Okay, okay!

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.460
You don't have to worry
about a thing, Marie-chan!

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:40.830
All right!

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.080
Let's enjoy our day
at the beach, guys!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.710
Right!

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:10.030
The ocean!

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:11.570
All right!

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.080
It's so pretty!

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.210
I'm getting to the beach first or bust!

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:26.670
Please tune in!

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.050
They're gonna
beat us to the beach!

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.550
Hey, you! Hold up!

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.060
Ah, youth.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:56.120
- I'm getting goosebumps!
- Not yet? Not yet?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.660
Senpai!

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.790
Yes!

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:02.790
Yeah!

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.460
You guys were waiting for us?

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.960
W-Why are you still here?

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.090
You should've gone
into the water first!

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.260
Summer is...

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.090
great!

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:16.260
Surrounded by all these
adorable mermaids...

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:19.600
this just might be my
chance for a summer fling!

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.470
Oh no, it's not!

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.020
What's up with this outfit?

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.400
Could it have less cloth?

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:29.520
Yes!

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.530
My choice of swimsuit
was on the money!

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.360
Why, you...

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.570
there you go again!

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.700
Who could this cool beauty be?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:39.950
That's Marie.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.460
By any chance, is she
your girlfriend, Sensei?

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.580
Man, you really
get around, you bad boy!

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.880
What is this? It's moving.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.210
Plus, it's talking.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.960
What is it made of?

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:56.260
Half of me is
made of gentleness.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.470
Yes, indeed!

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.470
Then what about the other half?

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.730
Teddie fur, that's what!

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.980
Gentleness and fur?

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.770
Who is that girl?

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:14.190
Risette, that girl is Marie-chan,
and she's with Yu...

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.110
With him?

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.030
I know this person.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.120
Margaret told me all about her.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.450
"Impossible, don't like her,
too rebellious..." That one.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:23.410
That sounds about right.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.660
You're wrong!

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.080
You're such a drag!

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.250
Senpai!

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.930
Dude... what's up with that?

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:41.050
Black is in, didn't you know?

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.390
I don't mean the color!
It's too graphic!

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:46.020
It totally makes your mind
go places it shouldn't!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.230
Hey, I'm not seeing anything.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.240
You're the only one saying that!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.570
Oh, shut up! Anyone can
see that it's messed up!

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:54.530
Hey, Sensei, let's leave those
guys and hit the water first!

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:56.320
Wait, Kanji, why aren't you
getting a nosebleed over me?

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.530
Good idea.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.610
Okay, I'm going on ahead!

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.110
Why would I do that?

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.530
Let's mermaid!

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.830
Woo hoo!

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.290
Hey, wait for us!

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.290
Wait! We have to stretch first!

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.250
Let's go, too.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.540
Uh, okay.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.130
No fair!

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.130
Hey! No jumping the gun!

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.090
All right!

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:16.670
Let's go!

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:38.030
Man, I'm starving.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:41.030
Let's have lunch when
those guys come out.

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:42.200
Yeah, let's do that.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.580
My strings are coming undone!

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.950
Hey, Teddie! What do you
think you're doing?

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:49.330
Don't be so stingy!

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.290
Just be bold and let it fall off...

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.880
That Teddie...

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:55.630
Hey, I caught a stylish mermaid!

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:57.760
What do you think
you're doing, damn you?

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.420
Oops, I messed up!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:01.840
What are they doing,
for Pete's sake?

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.060
Senpai! You're not
gonna believe this...

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.390
This stupid bear...

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:11.060
H-Hey... Hey... Hey!

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.190
What the hell do you
think you're doing?

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:15.610
Your boys are...

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:17.940
My boys?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.240
Hey, I'm the one who's flashing!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.740
That's what you're
modest about?

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.410
Cover up down there!

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.700
Oh, right.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.000
Hey, stop squirming!

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.830
If I lose you, I'm a dead man!

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.830
Nooooo!

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:44.680
I can't take it anymore!

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:48.010
Marie-chan, you can
really hold your breath.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.520
Hey, there's something
weird in the water.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.020
Something weird?

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.100
A sea slug?

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.230
Oh, man...

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.560
I can see the Pearly Gates...

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.190
Don't die, Teddie!

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.650
Hey, Teddie,
don't wilt like that!

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.650
We've got to cover it up
with something...

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.360
Senpai!

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.120
Oh crap, they're all coming back!

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.700
Wh-What am I
gonna do? Dammit...

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:12.790
This is all your fault, you know.
Gimme your trunks, dammit!

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.870
No, no, please stop!
Forgive me!

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.540
C-Cut it out, Kanji!

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:19.380
Or we'll really be
headed for disaster!

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:21.590
Kanji!

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:22.510
Take this!

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.140
What are you guys up...?

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:36.690
This is... You see...

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.270
It's the Birth of Venus...

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:39.820
Just kidding.

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.440
I-I really will be born, dammit!

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.700
Pervert!

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:51.160
Did that work out?

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:52.620
Anyway...

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.000
I'm itchy.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.530
Thanks for waiting!

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.390
Sorry to keep you waiting...

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:03.170
Let's dig in!

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:07.890
Yummy!

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.430
Senpai, I didn't know
you were a great cook!

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:12.600
This is delicious!

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.690
I knew I made the right
call, leaving it to you!

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:19.150
M-Marie-chan, do you cook?

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.230
No, I don't.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:25.650
Come to think of it, we still haven't
asked you about yourself, Marie-chan.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:28.620
You're Yu's friend from
his old school, right?

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.830
So are you the same age as us?

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.290
What school did you go to?

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:33.910
What school?

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.410
Did you say you lived
around here now?

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.330
How did you get here today?

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:39.830
What? How did I...?

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:41.000
You guys, listen...

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.880
Anyway, "Marie" sounds like
a foreign name, doesn't it?

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.760
What's your last name?

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:49.970
I want to know more
about you, Marie-chan!

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:52.600
Who cares about
that kind of stuff?

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:07.570
Marie-chan...

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:09.660
I'll go after her.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.410
You think we fired
too many questions at her?

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.760
None of them mean any harm.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:31.430
They just don't know
about your memories...

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.390
You don't have to tell me that...

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:40.400
Is it so wrong not to
have any memories?

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:47.110
Even if I don't have any memories, it's fun
to go around seeing things with you all.

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:48.650
Like today...

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.320
But...

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:53.330
Listen...

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:54.580
I'm sorry.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.580
Yu!

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.160
Marie-chan!

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:02.960
Sorry about that.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.050
Asking you all those questions.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.090
It's because this
one has no derriere!

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:10.590
I think the word is delicacy!

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.390
Kanji's butt is one big derriere!

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.430
D-Don't gimme that crap!

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.810
Have you ever seen my butt?

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.350
That's what it means
not to have any delicacy!

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:25.270
A derriere with no delicacy...

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:31.030
Amagi-senpai...

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:33.660
And there she goes with
another laughing fit!

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:34.740
Yep.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:45.090
A lot happened today,
but it sure was fun!

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:46.960
Yeah, like the Birth of Venus.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.960
Don't remind me, bro!

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.010
I'm still itchy.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:56.510
Well, hey, that's part of this
page from our youth, too!

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.270
Youth?

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.190
Hey, what's youth?

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:04.770
Huh? Uh...

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:07.610
Hanging with everybody
like we did today...

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:11.190
Confiding in each other
about what's bugging us.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:14.910
Why do you experience youth?
Because you have nothing to do?

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.280
No...

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.540
I mean, it's fun, you know?

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:22.410
Being with people
who see the real you.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.040
The real you...

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.380
Why am I getting
all philosophical?

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:34.760
Nah, nothing wrong
with that, right?

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.600
I have fun hanging out
with you guys, too.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.560
I mean, I even came to
the beach, which is so not me.

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:44.350
Yeah, you're right, you're not
the beach type, are you?

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:48.820
But it actually might be more fun
to do stuff that's out of character.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:50.440
Yeah, maybe.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:55.070
After all, "character" is like
a wall you throw up yourself.

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:58.530
Well, but I'm sure it's easier
to just stay inside that wall.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:13:59.740
Right.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:02.160
Easy and fun are
two different things.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:07.080
Oh, man! I'm totally
baring my soul, aren't I?

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:09.090
Bare it to your heart's content.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:29.940
What makes me different
from those people?

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:32.730
Is it because...
I'm getting off easy?

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:36.450
I'm sure you noticed it yourself.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:39.240
That they were all
facing who they really are.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:41.700
I saw that.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:44.250
But is that really necessary?

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.880
Then why don't you
ask them yourself?

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.380
Myself...

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:02.680
Hey, Marie-chan, what is this?

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:10.190
<i>What does it mean to face who you really are?</i>

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:10.730
You trying to get me
to bare my soul again?

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:22.080
<i>What do you think of the phrase "Pure Disappointment?"</i>

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:15.530
I don't think anything of it!

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:20.070
Hanamura, stop fooling around and do your
homework, or you'll miss the fireworks!

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:21.830
I know, I know!

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:25.370
Anyway, I was wondering
why you needed a video camera.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:27.210
So this was it, huh?

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:31.290
That's a display model,
by the way, so handle it with care!

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:42.050
<i>What does it mean to face who you really are?</i>

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.300
Whaaat?

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:40.470
D-Don't think about it!
You gotta feel it!

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:42.050
Just kidding.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:51.060
<i>Is meat-flavored gum really good?</i>

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:46.470
You better believe it is!

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:50.230
Here, a special bonus
for a beefsteak lover!

00:15:52.940 --> 00:16:00.070
<i>What does it mean to face who you really are?</i>

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.820
Let me see...
That's a hard one...

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:06.450
<i>What are you making?</i>

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:06.080
As you can see,
it's somen noodles.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:11.330
<i>Hello</i>

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.750
Hello, I'm Nanako Dojima.

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.630
I don't think that's a question for grade schoolers.

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:18.840
<i>What does it mean to face who you really are?</i>

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:19.880
What the hell...

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.590
I'm concentrating right now,
so hold up a second!

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:22.090
Yay!

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:28.930
<i>Is that the birth of a masterpiece?</i>

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:25.850
Right, birth...

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:26.600
Birth! Birth!

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.930
Hey! Don't remind me, dammit!

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:39.320
<i>What does it mean to face who you really are?</i>

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:35.610
Whaaat?

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:40.030
Excuse me, but could you
go through my agency for interviews?

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:44.950
<i>Not happening... bad news... you're such a slacker!</i>

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:44.930
No, that's "not happening...
I hate you... what a drag!"

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:56.460
<i>What does it mean to face who you really are?</i>

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:51.830
Yes, well, I'm very keen on
the quality of the material.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:56.460
Glasses must be flexible enough
to withstand violent movement, after all.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:17:06.430
<i>Would you call that your pride as a glasses craftsman?</i>

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:02.360
It's not so much
pride as conviction.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:06.430
If you compromise on glasses,
then you get what you paid for...

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.060
Done with my homework!

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:11.430
That's not what you get
when design is the focal point.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.020
I'm done, too!

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.440
Everybody, good job!

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:14.600
It was our pursuit of functionality
that led to the addition of a protector

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.400
All right!

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.360
Let's go see the fireworks!

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.560
to guard the area around
the nose and mouth.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.770
Nanako-chan, I'll help you
put on your yukata.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:17.770
Good glasses equal
functionality, you see.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.320
How did it go?

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:18.860
You don't mind?

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:21.240
You're getting all dressed up,
huh, Nanako-chan?

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:23.200
Do you know where your
dad put away your yukata?

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.950
I don't know...

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:23.950
Yes!

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:47.140
Tamaya!

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:49.970
Kumaya!

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:54.620
Kumaya!

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.110
No, no! Don't let it
rub off on you!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:12.750
You guys, don't party
all night, okay?

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.420
Nana-chan... bye-bye!

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:18.290
Bye-bye!

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:19.830
Good night!

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:20.450
See ya!

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.670
Bye-bye!

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:25.340
I don't know...

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:27.720
Feels like summer's
over now, huh?

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:29.890
Please don't say stuff like that...

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:33.220
Summer vacation was
really fun this year...

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:41.020
I had a feeling
it might come to this!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:42.190
Teddie!

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:44.070
Ta-da!

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:48.200
Let's start making our last
memories of summer vacation!

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:57.080
Who forgot this?

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:02.380
How do I turn this thing off?

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:05.550
Dad! How do I
get this yukata off?

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:08.340
Oh, hey, hang on a second!

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:10.180
<i>I know, I know!</i>

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:13.680
<i>Anyway, I was wondering
why you needed a video camera.</i>

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.350
<i>So this was it, huh?</i>

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:19.850
<i>That's a display model,
by the way, so handle it with care!</i>

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:22.480
<i>Who I really am, huh?</i>

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:27.240
<i>You know, I have a feeling this is
gonna get a little embarrassing again...</i>

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:32.280
<i>Before I got to be friends with these guys,
living in the sticks was so boring and annoying...</i>

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:35.660
<i>I had to tiptoe around other people...
and I was spinning my wheels...</i>

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:41.040
<i>But if you don't acknowledge that that's
who you are, too, you can never change, right?</i>

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:47.550
<i>I think I would've rotted away without ever realizing
that this is a great place, and everyone here is awesome.</i>

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:51.340
<i>Even though she's
a friend I love dearly,</i>

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:55.890
<i>the truth is, deep inside me,
there were some pretty ugly thoughts...</i>

00:19:55.890 --> 00:20:00.100
<i>But now that I know
that it exists,</i>

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:04.440
<i>it seems like I can be more
confident about how I feel, you know?</i>

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:10.200
<i>I always thought I was a loser
for not living my own life.</i>

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:15.290
<i>But now I believe that
the worst thing you can do is</i>

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:19.080
<i>not to decide yourself whether
you're going to live that life or not.</i>

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:24.590
<i>Even if you say, "But you're
a guy!", this is who I am, okay?</i>

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:29.130
<i>I'm not planning on changing
who I am anytime soon, either.</i>

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:32.340
<i>Want me to make you
a knitted doll too?</i>

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:36.970
<i>I became an idol because
I hated my drab, gloomy self.</i>

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:42.450
<i>But now I want people to see
the real me, not the idol.</i>

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:46.070
<i>In the end, I think I was always
running away from myself.</i>

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.030
<i>But...</i>

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:50.990
<i>No matter who I am,
that's the real me.</i>

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:53.530
<i>As for me...</i>

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:56.240
<i>I just don't know who I really am.</i>

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:59.290
<i>You don't know who
you are either, right?</i>

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.460
<i>I see...</i>

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:04.330
<i>It's scary, huh?
It makes you uneasy, huh?</i>

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:06.750
<i>But I'm sure it'll be all right.</i>

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:10.590
<i>Because we've got
Sensei and the others.</i>

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:14.510
<i>Neither you nor I are alone.</i>

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:17.600
<i>So I'm sure we'll both find
our real selves someday!</i>

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:30.650
Summer vacation will be
over tomorrow, guys.

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:33.280
Wanna go skiing over winter break?

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:35.620
You're already
talking about winter?

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.330
How impatient are you?

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:41.330
You should come
with us, too, Marie-chan!

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:44.580
Sure... I'll go.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:46.250
I'm looking forward to it.

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:50.210
Hey, Marie-chan,
you're really into this!

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:52.880
I'd better come up
with a killer plan, then!

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:04.390
Let's go grab something to eat!

00:22:04.390 --> 00:22:05.900
Meat!

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:08.020
But the ingredients...

00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:08.480
Hey, listen.

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:12.940
Maybe I'll try to remember...

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:14.700
My memories.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.620
Yeah. I'll help you.

00:22:18.620 --> 00:22:20.700
Yes, will you?

00:22:20.990 --> 00:22:23.250
Because I don't know what to do.

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:25.420
Hey!

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:28.710
You two! We're gonna
leave you behind!

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:29.960
We'll be right there!

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:33.840
I'm counting on you, okay?

00:24:18.610 --> 00:24:20.160
What do you guys
think you're doing?

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:22.700
Why did you have to
bring that one up all of a sudden?

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:24.780
Marie-chan, are you
sure you don't mind?

00:24:24.780 --> 00:24:26.160
It's just the first day.

00:24:26.160 --> 00:24:27.160
No need to panic.

00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:28.830
Let's try hard tomorrow, too.
